# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# fz-mart TEST environment — copy to .env.test and fill in.
# Commit THIS file (.env.test.example); never commit .env.test.
#
# Values here OVERRIDE .env for the Playwright suite only. Anything you
# leave out falls back to .env, so only list what must differ.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required: a THROWAWAY database ───────────────────────────────
# The E2E suite writes to this DB on every run: it creates an OWNER admin
# user, upserts shipping zone 1, flips the `payments` settings group into
# MOCK mode, creates an E2E100 coupon, and races real checkouts that
# decrement stock. None of that may ever touch a store with real orders.
#
# Local MySQL 8 (this project's chosen setup):
#   1. Install MySQL 8 for Windows (installer or `winget install Oracle.MySQL`).
#   2. Create the database and a user for it:
#        CREATE DATABASE fz_mart_test;
#        CREATE USER 'fzmart_test'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'choose-a-password';
#        GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON fz_mart_test.* TO 'fzmart_test'@'localhost';
#        FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
#   3. Put the matching URL below.
#   4. Apply the schema:  npm run db:migrate:test
#
# The suite REFUSES to run if this points at a hosted/production host
# (tidbcloud.com, planetscale, rds.amazonaws.com, …) or matches the
# DATABASE_URL in .env — see tests/e2e/helpers/guard.ts.
DATABASE_URL="mysql://fzmart_test:choose-a-password@localhost:3306/fz_mart_test"

# ── Redis (currently SHARED with .env by choice) ──────────────────
# Left unset on purpose: tests fall back to the REDIS_URL in .env.
# global-setup deletes `ratelimit:checkout:*` and `ratelimit:login:*` keys,
# which are ephemeral counters, so the blast radius is small — but it IS
# still your production Upstash instance.
#
# To separate it later, uncomment and point at a second Upstash DB or a
# local Redis. Nothing else needs to change.
# REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"
